{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789833922,"nonce":"v8hBFvguhNSQNbQPuXiq6mtBHF8=","title":"Python inference: a parameter type crossed one call per round","message":"`infer_module` collected the argument types every call passed and\njoined them into the callees' parameters only at the end of a round, so\na type reaching a callee through a chain of calls took a round per link:\nrichards converged in 7 inner rounds, three times over (the outer loop\nrestarts from the declared layouts once the globals settle), 24 full\npasses over 53 functions, 21 ms of the 31 ms parse phase (NUC).\n\nNow a round is a worklist: every item once, the module body, then each\nitem a call typed a parameter of since it was inferred, until none is\nleft. Field writes are gathered per item so a re-inferred item replaces\nits earlier reading. Rounds: richards 7 -\u003e 4, others 5 -\u003e 3 and 2.\n\nAlso: the outer loop skips the methods-settling round when the settled\nround found no dynamic method (its inputs would be identical); only\nfunctions that declare a `global` are re-read for the globals' types;\nthe frontend's tables hash with FxHash (SipHash on String keys was a\nfifth of inference); a body's `Scope` is cached by address for the run\nof one program; `ZYNTAX_TRACE_LOWER_PHASES=1` times the frontend's\nsteps too.\n\nrichards parse 31 -\u003e 17 ms; parse+compile on the NUC now fannkuch 22,\nfloat 24, nbody 39, richards 46, meteor 39, nqueens 43 ms.","files":null}]}